# Offline pin notes — gpw-mbd-forces

## Policy

CP2K 2026.1 stock `PAIR_POTENTIAL TYPE` has **no MBD**. Oracle is **libMBD**
(same as `gpw-mbd-ice`): energy pin from Fortran `cmbd_mbd_scs_energy`; forces
dual-gated as product \(\nabla E\) vs independent central FD of that energy.

## Geometry

Water dimer (Å), isolated free-atom MBD@rsSCS (β=0.83, a=6):

```
O  0.000000  0.000000  0.000000
H  0.758602  0.000000  0.504284
H  0.758602  0.000000 -0.504284
O  3.000000  0.000000  0.000000
H  3.758602  0.000000  0.504284
H  3.758602  0.000000 -0.504284
```

Å→Bohr: `1/0.52917720859` (ATV).

## Energy pin

E_disp = −1.4928804171407961e-03 Ha (libMBD git 88069c6).

## Force dual-gate (never live in ctest)

```text
max |F_product − F_fd(h=1e-5)| ≤ 1e-6 Ha/Bohr
|sum F| ≤ 1e-8 Ha/Bohr
```

Optional host with libMBD C API: request `do_gradients` / force output on the
same coordinates and compare to ATV product forces (expect O(h²) agreement).
